    79	<p>All volumes, prices and costs are designed arithmetic, not market facts. <!-- CHECK: 03-prices --> Year one is intentionally a loss after charging the founder’s labour: it buys proof, not owner income. The mature design pays €100,000 for the founder role and retains €74,000 before company tax. That clears the reader’s income gate without pretending the owner works free.</p>
    80	<p>The working-capital rule is 50% of the company’s wholesale price at order, 40% after factory acceptance and 10% after site acceptance. A €17,500 deposit almost covers the assumed €18,000 hardware and assembly bill for one cell; two overlapping builds still require cash. After evidence, the maximum €100,000 allocation is €28,000 for a pre-production/demo cell and test packs, €32,000 working capital, €15,000 for insurance/legal/conformity documentation, €8,000 already spent on discovery and €17,000 contingency. No inventory beyond one critical-spares kit is justified until three paid installations pass.</p>
    81	</section>
    82	
    83	<section class="scale">
    84	<h2>From service to company</h2>
    85	<h3>How the cell works—and how it is accepted</h3>
    86	<p>The pack crosses a photoelectric trigger on a controlled single-file conveyor. A global-shutter monochrome camera freezes motion. Cross-polarised diffuse illumination suppresses specular glare from top film; a second low-angle light is tested only when embossed or wrinkled film defeats the first geometry. Lens and working distance are selected from the actual field of view so the thinnest character stroke has enough pixels at the fastest line speed. Those are recipe parameters, not settings an operator improvises.</p>
    87	<p>The algorithm first locates the print zone from stable pack features, then separates three questions. Presence asks whether ink exists in the expected region. OCR decodes the date and lot. Verification compares the decoded strings with values received from the authoritative line recipe, including allowed date arithmetic and format. “No read,” stale recipe, communications loss and low confidence all fail closed: reject this pack or stop after a configured sequence. A merely present, beautifully legible wrong date must fail.</p>
    88	<p>The PLC—not cloud software—tracks the pack from camera to reject. A pusher or air blast removes it; a downstream sensor confirms departure; bin-full, missed trigger, unconfirmed reject or encoder discrepancy stops the line. The integrator owns that deterministic state machine, guarding and restart behaviour. From 20 January 2027 the EU Machinery Regulation applies, and a party making a substantial modification can be treated as the manufacturer with conformity obligations for the affected machinery. <!-- CHECK: 03-machinery-date --><!-- CHECK: 03-substantial-mod --> That is why the vision company does not casually splice into a safety circuit or claim that a CE-marked camera makes a CE-compliant cell.</p>
    89	<p>Acceptance starts with a jointly signed defect taxonomy: missing print; stale or future date; transposed digit; incomplete character; weak contrast; smear; double print; displacement; glare; wrinkle; condensation; wrong lot format. The factory test runs 3,000 labelled defect images with zero misses, then a site test runs at least 100 physical challenge packs through trigger, decision, tracking and confirmed reject. A 10,000-good-pack production run must stay below the agreed false-reject rate—initial hurdle 0.2%—without bypass. Zero misses in an image library does not prove zero field risk, especially when images from one run are correlated. <!-- CHECK: 03-stat-test --> Results are reported by film, ribbon, line speed and defect class, not as one flattering accuracy percentage.</p>
    90	<p>Cleaning belongs in the design review. EU hygiene rules require relevant equipment and its installation to permit cleaning and, where necessary, disinfection. <!-- CHECK: 03-hygiene-law --> EHEDG describes five principles—material compatibility, cleanability, drainability, accessibility and segregation—and ISO 14159 covers hygiene requirements for machinery used where consumer risk can arise. <!-- CHECK: 03-ehedg-principles --><!-- CHECK: 03-iso-hygiene --> Even downstream of sealed food, the cell needs sloped stainless surfaces, accessible belt removal, sealed cable entries and documented chemical/temperature limits. An IP67 camera component is not a washdown design. The diagnostic observes the real cleaning method before selecting enclosure, connectors or fasteners.</p>
    91	
    92	<h3>First, fifth, twentieth</h3>
    93	<p><strong>Customer one</strong> consumes the founder. A rented camera and two lights go to the lab; the partner fabricates a one-off bracket and reject; the founder labels defects, tunes every region and stands through both shifts. The deliverable is not just a working cell. It is the first bill of materials, interface control document, defect library, FAT/SAT script, sanitation checklist, recipe schema and support runbook.</p>
    94	<p><strong>Customer five</strong> gets one of two standard conveyor widths, a fixed camera-to-pack envelope, prewired cabinet, versioned PLC handshakes for the two PLC families actually encountered, and a commissioning fixture that can replay triggers. The partner handles mechanical and electrical installation from drawings. A trained vision engineer performs most recipe work; the founder attends acceptance only for an exception. New film, ribbon, printer head or code format becomes a paid qualification, not free support.</p>
    95	<p><strong>Customer twenty</strong> arrives through a partner’s installed base. The partner performs survey, installation, Dutch operator training and first response. The company ships a tested module, reviews acceptance evidence remotely and handles optical/software escalation. Recurrence follows real state changes: new private-label SKUs, artwork and film changes, printer/ribbon changes, cleaning damage, lighting drift and retailer audit evidence. The accumulating asset is the consented, anonymised defect image set joined to film, lighting, lens, printer, speed and acceptance result—not generic “AI data.”</p>
    96	<p>The twentieth delivery is only materially different if written partner certification lets another person do most of it. Annual service without new SKUs, changed equipment, drift or evidence review is an invented annuity and should not be billed. At 36 supported lines, one support engineer plus partner first response is a design assumption to measure; if the founder still debugs night shifts, the mature economics are fiction.</p>
    97	</section>
    98	
    99	<section class="competition">
   100	<h2>The incumbent gets a turn</h2>
   101	<p>PackCheck is not a hypothetical future rival. Its Vi-Track material advertises recipe-controlled THT inspection, API control, ejection and a web dashboard; it also publishes a customer account in which Vezet selected the company to inspect film, codes and labels on vegetable bagging lines. <!-- CHECK: 03-packcheck-product --><!-- CHECK: 03-packcheck-case --> Vision Partners’ EVIS covers date, barcode, text and seal checks and connects to labeling software, MES and PLCs. <!-- CHECK: 03-evis-product --> Both are Dutch, local and broader than this proposal.</p>
   102	<p>Above them sit the printer vendors. Domino’s R-Series joins printers, cameras and lighting and offers to test a customer’s code on its product before commitment. <!-- CHECK: 03-domino-range-competition --> Videojet-Laetus already offers OCR/OCV, best-before and lot checks, printer synchronisation, SKU management, IP67 camera configurations and diffuse or polarised lighting. <!-- CHECK: 03-videojet-system-competition --> Below them sits the internal automation engineer with a Cognex or Keyence sensor. Taken together, these products cover nearly every functional box in the proposed cell; a generic OCR offer has no credible wedge. <!-- CHECK: 03-incumbent-inference --></p>
   103	<p>An incumbent response requires no new product. The printer vendor bundles vision into a replacement quote and uses one job setup for print and inspect. The local integrator copies the narrow validation script into its broader platform, adds film and seal inspection, and keeps the customer. The customer’s automation team accepts slightly more false rejects because the camera cost is small and support is already on site.</p>
   104	<p>Dutch integrators become channels only through a deliberately subordinate deal. The partner owns the end customer, mechanical and PLC scope, machinery-risk work, Dutch training and first-line SLA. The new company publishes a wholesale price, never sells directly into the partner’s registered accounts, supplies the code-specific module and validation, and receives contractual access to anonymised defect and performance data. The partner keeps roughly one-third of the end price in the hurdle model. If a partner will introduce prospects but refuses data rights, margin transparency or non-circumvention, it is not a channel; it is using free specialist presales before internalising the job.</p>
   105	</section>
   106	
   107	<div class="counter">
   108	<h2>The capable failure</h2>
   109	<p>The team executes well. Two cheese packers pay for diagnostics. The optical design passes on glossy film, the reject path survives site acceptance, operators like the evidence log, and a respected Dutch integrator sells five cells. Then the integrator learns which dome, lens and thresholds work, while Domino supplies a printer-linked camera in the next fleet refresh. Customers prefer one service number and one recipe entry. The partner recreates the defect checklist in its existing platform and offers seal and film checks alongside the date for a modest premium. It honours every contract, simply stops ordering the module.</p>
   110	<p>Nothing was stolen. OCR components were available, the acceptance procedure was observable, and five installations did not create enough diverse labelled failures to make the data asset indispensable. The founder built a competent subcontracted feature whose distributor owned acquisition, integration, service and trust. Good engineering accelerated the partner’s learning. This is the central structural risk, not “poor sales”: the channel required for language and scale is also the party best placed to capture the margin.</p>
   111	</div>
   112	
   113	<section class="monday">
   114	<h2>The first ninety days</h2>
   115	<ol>
   116	<li><strong>Write the one-page boundary.</strong> Fix pack form, printer technology, two fields, line position, maximum speed range, fail-closed behaviour and exclusions. Ask PackCheck, Vision Partners and one packaging-line service firm which sentence makes the offer redundant.</li>
   117	<li><strong>Secure one channel experiment.</strong> Offer Vision Partners first—then at most one other integrator—registered-account protection, 20% of diagnostics, a target wholesale schedule and first-line ownership. Require access to anonymised test/performance data and attendance at buyer interviews. No signed experiment by day 30 means no equipment purchase.</li>
   118	<li><strong>Run ten event interviews.</strong> Use the named screen, but continue only with plants that can produce a dated code escape, hold, complaint, audit action or upcoming line change. Record frequency, affected units, labour, downtime, retailer consequence, current control and signer. Do not pitch during the evidence half.</li>
   119	<li><strong>Sell two CodeProof diagnostics at €3,500 each.</strong> Payment, not a letter of interest, is the demand test. Rent camera, lens and lights; use customer packs; quote the €52,000 cell only after the defect and integration envelope is known.</li>
   120	<li><strong>Challenge the mechanism.</strong> Build the labelled defect set, compare lighting geometries, replay recipe mismatches and test the physical reject states with the partner. Produce the signed acceptance protocol and a fixed bill of materials before quoting.</li>
   121	<li><strong>Apply the gate.</strong> Spend at most €8,000 before evidence. Pass only if one integrator signs the channel experiment, two independent packers pay full diagnostic price, at least one line meets the optical test, and one buyer gives a conditional order at the price hurdle subject to site acceptance. Kill if any element is absent by day 90, if more than two optical/mechanical variants are needed, or if the partner will not leave the company the modelled margin and data rights.</li>
   122	</ol>
   123	</section>
   124	
   125	<div class="verdict-box">
   126	<h2>Verdict</h2>
   127	<p class="verdict">TEST THROUGH A PARTNER</p>
   128	<p>The single assumption that would most change the verdict is that Vision Partners, or one equivalent Dutch integrator, will repeatedly resell the narrow module while leaving its maker both the required wholesale contribution and rights to the validation data. Test that before the camera.</p>
   129	</div>
   130	
   131	<div class="reading">
   132	<h2>Reading</h2>
   133	<ul>
   134	<li>European Union, <a href="https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/PDF/?from=EN&amp;uri=CELEX%3A32011R1169">Regulation (EU) No 1169/2011</a>, Article 24 and Annex X; and <a href="https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dir/2011/91/oj/eng">Directive 2011/91/EU</a>, Articles 1–4.</li>
   135	<li>NVWA, <a href="https://www.nvwa.nl/onderwerpen/voedselveiligheid/etikettering-van-levensmiddelen/houdbaarheidsdatum-levensmiddelen">“Houdbaarheidsdatum op levensmiddelen”</a> and the <a href="https://www.nvwa.nl/documenten/2025/12/19/veiligheidswaarschuwing-upfront-pitas-en-wraps">19 December 2025 Upfront safety warning</a>.</li>
   136	<li>European Union, <a href="https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2004/852/oj/eng">Regulation (EC) No 852/2004</a>, Annex II, on hygiene and cleanability.</li>
   137	<li>ISO, <a href="https://www.iso.org/standard/23748.html">ISO 14159:2002</a>; EHEDG, <a href="https://www.ehedg.org/congress-2026/programm-sessions/speakers/session/day1-main-stage-jurgen-hoffman">the five hygienic-design principles</a>.</li>
   138	<li>European Union, <a href="https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2023/1230/en">Regulation (EU) 2023/1230 on machinery</a>, Articles 18 and 54.</li>
   139	<li>Cognex, <a href="https://www.cognex.com/support/downloads/ns/1/11/35/In-Sight%203800%20Datasheet.pdf">In-Sight 3800 datasheet</a> and <a href="https://docs.cognex.com/isvs_2530/web/EN/is3800-manual/Content/Topics/specifications/imager-3800.htm?TocPath=Specifications%7C_____2">current specifications</a>.</li>
   140	<li>Domino, <a href="https://www.domino-printing.com/en-us/products/r-series">R-Series code inspection</a>; Videojet-Laetus, <a href="https://www.videojet.com/us/homepage/products/vision-systems.html">inline vision systems</a>.</li>
   141	<li>PackCheck, <a href="https://packcheck.nl/vitrack-platform/">Vi-Track Platform</a>; Vision Partners, <a href="https://visionpartners.nl/en/products/evis-label-packaging-inspection-system/">EVIS</a>.</li>
   142	</ul>
   143	</div>
   144	
